[center][size=5][i][color=#efe6d6]Ever wanted to go on a dyeing spree, not limited to what you have equipped?[/color][/i][/size]

[size=3][color=#a89a86]That's why this mod exists. The camp dyer only shows what you are wearing: to dye a stored piece you leave, equip it, come back, dye, and put it away again. [b]Dye All[/b] lists [b]every dyeable item you own[/b] right on the dye screen and puts any of them on for you, without ever leaving the menu.[/color][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][color=#c9a45c][b]FEATURES[/b][/color][/size]

[color=#b3262e][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]Everything in one list.[/b] Bag, wardrobe, private chest and warehouse, sorted by type, name or location.
[color=#e0a12f][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]One double-click.[/b] The item goes on and the dyer shows it immediately. No menu exits, no tab switching.
[color=#2f6f9a][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]Dye in a row.[/b] Pick colors, pick the next item: your colors are applied first and the dye screen stays open.
[color=#4f9a7c][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]All gear.[/b] Armor, cloaks, weapons, shields, horse gear and A.T.A.G. parts.
[color=#7a2f6d][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]Puts itself away.[/b] Close the dyer and everything goes back after 10 seconds: your own gear on, each dyed piece back where it came from.
[color=#d2532f][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]Full bag? No problem.[/b] Items go on straight from storage.
[color=#e9dcc2][size=4]■[/size][/color]  [b]Plays fair.[/b] Never makes an item dyeable that the game doesn't allow, and the dyer charges its normal price.

[line]

[size=5][color=#c9a45c][b]HOW TO USE[/b][/color][/size]

[color=#c9a45c][b]1[/b][/color]   At a camp dyer, choose [b]Dye[/b]. The Dye All panel appears on the right.
[color=#c9a45c][b]2[/b][/color]   Double-click the item you want. Horse gear: [b]RB[/b] to the horse tab. A.T.A.G. parts: [b]RB[/b] twice.
[color=#c9a45c][b]3[/b][/color]   Pick colors, then double-click the next item. For the last one, press Dye.
[color=#c9a45c][b]4[/b][/color]   Close the dye screen. Everything goes back on its own.

[color=#a89a86][i]F7 shows the panel anywhere; F7 or Esc gives the mouse back to the game.[/i][/color]

[line]

[size=5][color=#c9a45c][b]INSTALL[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Requires [b]Crimson Desert 1.0.0.3663[/b].
[*]With [b]DMM[/b]: drag the zip onto DMM, enable [b]DyeAll[/b] on the ASI tab, mount, start the game.
[*]To remove: disable or remove DyeAll in DMM.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#c9a45c][b]SAFETY[/b][/color][/size]

The mod only uses the game's own move, equip and dye requests, one step at a time, and checks your inventories after each one. If a step fails it stops and tells you: the item is either worn or in your bag, [b]never lost[/b]. Backing up your save before first use is still a good idea.

After a game update the mod checks the game's code before every hook and switches off whatever no longer matches instead of guessing. Wait for an update in that case.

[line]

[size=5][color=#c9a45c][b]GOOD TO KNOW[/b][/color][/size]

[spoiler]
[b]What does it cost?[/b]
The dyer's normal price, once per item. The game charges per Dye press, and the mod presses it for each item in your spree.

[b]Why are some items greyed out?[/b]
Crossbows: no character has a slot for them. A.T.A.G. parts: the dyer only has an A.T.A.G. tab once you own an A.T.A.G.

[b]A weapon went straight back?[/b]
Your current character can't use it, so the game refuses it and the mod returns it to where it came from.

[b]The dyer's list looks out of date.[/b]
Press [b]Refresh[/b] in the panel (or RB then LB).
[/spoiler]

[line]

[size=5][color=#c9a45c][b]FOUND A BUG?[/b][/color][/size]

Post in the comments or the Bugs tab and attach [b]DyeAll.log[/b] from the game's [i]bin64[/i] folder, taken right after it happened. It records every step the mod took.

[line]

